       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 2400 mg per dose four times daily comes to 9,600 mg/day, which is three times the maximum labeled ibuprofen dose for adults (3,200 mg/day, and usually 1,200 mg/day or less for OTC use). A single 2,400 mg dose is also well above the usual 800 mg per-dose ceiling. That much ibuprofen carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day total)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n\nIf 2,400 mg per dose four times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
