       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day is three times the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it, and I don't think I can safely put it into the system. The risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, metabolic acidosis and CNS effects is high, and extra monitoring wouldn't make the dose safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is the likely intended regimen if the total daily dose was meant\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute labeled maximum, with a note for GI protection and renal monitoring\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I can enter adjuncts instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen, or a different agent of your choice.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol or trial, please work it out directly with pharmacy. I can't be the one to enter it."
